Just a small note for those who've shown concern over the slowdown
in H&S releases lately.  Without spewing my problems, in summary,
my life has been hell.  My wife and I moved in with my inlaws to
start building our home.  Here we are 4 months later, and rather
than getting ready to move in to our new home, we're scheduling
court dates with lawyers because a lawyer didn't do his job 2 years
ago when we bought our land.  Needless to say, I've been busy as hell,
and haven't had a whole lot of ambition to work on H&S, or anything
else for that matter.  My wife and I plan to cut our losses and walk
away if things don't pan out soon, so I don't expect to be in this slump
much longer.  Hang in there!

Oh, not to mention a minor setback Rob had with his castle designing.
He lost the source in a HD swap, and the backup was corrupt.  Fortunately
we keep copies of each other's code!  He lost a few weeks worth of work,
but that's better than losing everything!

Enough with our misery, enjoy the game.  I hope this version is more stable.
